    "prompt_tokens": 227,
    "raw": "Given that the wholesale club sells ground beef in 5-pound packages and Maurice purchases 4 packages, he has a total of \\(4 \\times 5 = 20\\) pounds of ground beef. Maurice plans to make one 2-pound burger for each person attending, including himself. Let's denote the number of people Maurice can invite as \\(x\\). Since Maurice will also have a burger, the total number of burgers needed is \\(x + 1\\). Each burger requires 2 pounds of ground beef, so the total ground beef required is \\(2(x + 1)\\) pounds. Setting this equal to the total ground beef Maurice has, we get:\n\\[2(x + 1) = 20\\]\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\\[x + 1 = 10\\]\nSubtracting 1 from both sides, we find:\n\\[x = 9\\]\nSo, Maurice can invite 9 people. Including himself, the total number of people is \\(9 + 1 = 10\\).\n\nChecking the result: Maurice has 20 pounds of ground beef, and 10 people will each have a 2-pound burger, which totals \\(10 \\times 2 = 20\\) pounds. This matches the amount of ground beef Maurice has.\n\nFINAL: 9",
